00-first: reading="Remember which books you read during the year and what you thought of them, in one simple place." focused={"id":"scope","text":"Should this cover only books read in the current year, or become an ongoing record across years?"}
00-first: reading="Find a way to keep onboarding emails without making new users feel spammed, while addressing the rising unsubscribe rate and preserving marketing’s value from the sequence." focused={"id":"model-3ab2261f0835cbdd","text":"Should the main success measure be reducing the unsubscribe rate, reducing the feeling of being spammed, or balancing both equally?"}
00-first: reading="Learners should leave a wrong answer feeling smarter rather than dumber, by understanding what went wrong and receiving a supportive explanation without adding unwanted complexity." focused={"id":"model-d32e9d137a0e7e42","text":"When a learner gets an answer wrong, is the most important change that they understand the mistake, feel less judged, or both?"}
00-first: reading="Know within about five seconds each morning whether yesterday went well, primarily through useful changes per hour, while making job failures visible before they go unnoticed." focused={"id":"well-definition","text":"What specifically should make yesterday count as having gone well: a target or threshold for useful changes per hour, a comparison with another day, or something else?"}
01-answer: reading="Know within about five seconds each morning whether yesterday went well, with useful changes per hour as the main signal, a failed 6am job overriding the result, and cost shown only when it is unusually high." focused=null
00-first: reading="Make starting nighttime thought dumps easier, possibly by using voice, reducing terminal friction, or both." focused={"id":"model-314eff6ee31b8fc2","text":"Which matters more to solve first: talking being faster than typing when tired, or opening a terminal feeling like work?"}
00-first: reading="A human-first system that compounds its own value while coordinating the full agentic software-development lifecycle—from brain dump, prompt, hunch, or intuition to a durable, verified, human-review-ready PR—while improving the health of the codebase and making the next change easier." focused={"id":"model-331ff49ee2e54440","text":"Is the true goal primarily the end-to-end experience and quality of the resulting PR, with the board/meta-harness as the means—or is building that board/meta-harness itself equally part of the goal?"}
